          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of King David</strong><br>\nDavid was born in Bethlehem, the youngest son of Jesse. As a young boy, he tended his father's sheep, a job considered the lowest of work in his society. David was skilled with a sling, which he used to protect his flock. His musical talents with the harp brought him to the attention of King Saul, who sought relief from his tormenting spirits through music.</p>\n\n<p><strong>David and Goliath</strong><br>\nDavid's courage became legendary when he faced Goliath, a giant warrior who challenged the Israelites. While the entire Israelite army hesitated, David, with only a sling and a stone, defeated Goliath. His victory showcased his bravery and his faith in God, which later became inspirational in Jewish, Christian, and Islamic traditions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Saul's Jealousy</strong><br>\nAfter defeating Goliath, David became a hero in Israel. His growing popularity sparked King Saul's jealousy, leading to David's persecution. Saul's relentless pursuit forced David to flee and live as an outlaw. Despite Saul's hostility, David spared Saul's life on two occasions, demonstrating his loyalty to the king he was destined to succeed.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
